# [[ .Name ]]

A [Crossplane](https://crossplane.io) composition function in C, compiled to a
wasip1 reactor of about 70 KB by `zig cc` and run by
[function-wasm](https://github.com/jonasz-lasut/function-wasm). No wasi-sdk:
the one `zig` binary is the C toolchain, the build system and the package
fetcher.

- `proto/run_function.proto` is crossplane's `RunFunction` contract, vendored
  (with the `google/protobuf` types it imports); `zig build gen-proto` compiles
  it with [nanopb](https://jpa.kapsi.fi/nanopb/)'s generator (`pip install
  nanopb`) into `src/fnv1`, which is checked in so a plain `zig build` needs
  only zig. The `.options` files beside the protos make every string, map and
  repeated field heap allocated, so no field is bounded by the codec.
- `src/fn.c` - `run_function` over the generated structs (edit this).
  `src/structpb.h` reads and builds `google.protobuf.Struct` values (the
  Input's `config`, every resource); `src/wasmfn.h` is the function-wasm
  [ABI](https://github.com/jonasz-lasut/function-wasm/blob/main/docs/abi.md)
  glue: the `wasmfn_alloc` / `wasmfn_run` exports, the handle (decode, run,
  encode; errors become fatal results), the `wasmfn.log` logger and the
  `wasmfn.http` client. Only the exports and the host imports are
  wasi-specific, so `zig build test` runs `src/fn_test.c` natively (a fake host
  is installed for the `wasmfn.http` tests). `config.greetingUrl` fetches the
  greeting through the host, within the egress grant of the module's manifest.
- `build.zig` builds both (a wasm32-wasi reactor and the native test binary)
  from the same sources, nanopb and cJSON from `build.zig.zon`.

```shell
# Unit tests run natively.
zig build test

# Compile to a wasip1 module.
guestfn build                       # zig build -Doptimize=ReleaseSmall → fn.wasm

# Publish it as an OCI artifact; it prints the module block for the Composition.
guestfn push ghcr.io/example/[[ .Name ]]:v0.1.0
```

Reference the module from a Composition step of function-wasm:

```yaml
- step: [[ .Name ]]
  functionRef:
    name: function-wasm
  input:
    apiVersion: wasm.fn.crossplane.io/v1beta1
    kind: Input
    module:
      type: OCI
      oci:                     # printed by guestfn push
        ref: ghcr.io/example/[[ .Name ]]:v0.1.0@sha256:<manifest digest>
    config:
      greeting: hi
```

`example/` renders locally with the function-wasm runtime serving this
directory (`--module-dir`) and `crossplane render`:

```shell
guestfn build
crossplane render example/xr.yaml example/composition.yaml example/functions.yaml
```
